ITEM F14: MODIS PROBE WITH ELEVATION CONTROL & SIGN PREDICTION
================================================================================
1. Physical Sign Prediction (Stated Prior to Computation):
   - Cold-air pooling mechanism: Nocturnal drainage causes dense cold air to accumulate in topographic hollows and valley floors (low TPI), while flanking ridges (high TPI) remain warmer. This predicts a POSITIVE correlation between TPI and LST: r(TPI, LST) > 0.
   - Environmental lapse rate mechanism: Higher absolute elevations are colder due to atmospheric expansion: r(elevation, LST) < 0.
   - Confounding interaction: Because ridges (high TPI) generally sit at higher absolute elevation (z), the lapse rate (cooling with elevation) and cold-air pooling (warming on ridges) oppose each other and partly cancel in raw correlation.
   - Methodological isolation: To isolate microclimatic pooling, LST must first be regressed on absolute SRTM elevation across valid pixels (LST = alpha + beta * elev), and the partial correlation between the residual LST (epsilon) and TPI must be computed: r_partial = r(epsilon, TPI).
   - Sign expectation: If cold-air pooling operates, r_partial MUST BE POSITIVE (valleys colder than expected for their elevation, ridges warmer than expected), and stronger on decoupled nights than on coupled nights.

2. Elevation-Controlled Probe Results on the 3 Closed-Canopy Sinks (F12 Dataset):
   - Node 1: Kudremukh / Chikmagalur (13.25°N, 75.50°E) [Within-cell TPI range 485.2 m]
     * Decoupled (N=6 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 376 | Elev Slope beta = +0.74 °C/km (std 1.88) | Raw r = +0.141 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = +0.074 (std 0.137)
     * Coupled   (N=4 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 294 | Elev Slope beta = +0.25 °C/km (std 3.49) | Raw r = +0.067 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = +0.145 (std 0.244)
   - Node 2: Ratnagiri / Koyna Gorge (17.25°N, 73.75°E) [Within-cell TPI range 378.3 m]
     * Decoupled (N=3 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 270 | Elev Slope beta = +0.51 °C/km (std 5.45) | Raw r = -0.019 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = +0.046 (std 0.324)
     * Coupled   (N=7 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 187 | Elev Slope beta = -0.15 °C/km (std 2.96) | Raw r = +0.027 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = -0.004 (std 0.284)
   - Node 3: Kali River Canyon (14.75°N, 74.25°E) [Within-cell TPI range 364.8 m]
     * Decoupled (N=5 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 154 | Elev Slope beta = +0.82 °C/km (std 1.54) | Raw r = +0.083 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = +0.064 (std 0.081)
     * Coupled   (N=6 nights): Mean Valid Pixels = 101 | Elev Slope beta = -0.69 °C/km (std 6.02) | Raw r = +0.035 | Partial r(TPI, residual) = -0.011 (std 0.177)

   POOLED CLOSED-CANOPY RESULTS (F14):
